272
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:32,760
He's really funny.

273
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:36,620
Like, the other day, he made up this joke:

274
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,160
What's green and says,

275
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:41,000
"Hey, I'm a frog"?

276
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:43,700
A talking frog.

277
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,700
Oh, no, you can't have him, he's too funny.

278
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,740
Well, all right, that's fine. What about Leslie?

279
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,780
Oh, no, no, not Leslie. No.

280
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,360
She's the only one that knows

281
00:13:57,360 --> 00:13:58,540
how to burp the alphabet.

282
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,460
All right, so that leaves Chandler.

283
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:03,800
No, no, you can't have Chandler.

284
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:06,160
No, no. She's my little genius.

285
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,980
I got big hopes for her.

286
00:14:07,980 --> 00:14:11,260
She's gonna be a doctor or a realtor.

287
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:17,280
Wow, Frank, I think we just ran out of kids.

288
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:20,980
Oh, I think you're right.

289
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,480
Oh, wow. Phoebe,

290
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:28,500
I don't think I can give one of them up.

291
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:30,740
I mean, you know, they drive me crazy,

292
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:31,840
but they're my babies.

293
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:36,460
I'm sorry, Frank,

294
00:14:36,460 --> 00:14:38,480
I didn't realize things were so bad.

295
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,400
You know, I'll help out more.

296
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,420
I can baby-sit anytime you want.

297
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:43,880
You name the day and I'll be there.

298
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:44,820
How about tomorrow?

299
00:14:44,860 --> 00:14:45,780
Well, that's not good.

300
00:14:47,780 --> 00:14:50,640
But I can move some stuff around and I'll be there.

301
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,700
You and Alice just take the whole day together.

302
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:55,160
You'd do that for us?

303
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,180
Are you kidding?

304
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:57,500
That's what sisters are for.

305
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,840
Oh, look at them.

306
00:15:07,160 --> 00:15:09,160
I love you so much.

307
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,680
Oh, crap, don't wake up...

308
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:17,720
Where are Bill and Colleen?

309
00:15:17,820 --> 00:15:19,720
They are in the kitchen, getting something to eat.

310
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,400
Can you believe how nice they are?

311
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,440
We have to leave.

312
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,480
Why? What did you do in the bathroom?

313
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,000
I didn't get to the bathroom.

314
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:30,360
I bumped into Owen on the way.

315
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:31,940
He didn't know he was adopted.

316
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,260
There's a slight chance...

317
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:34,580
...l may have told him.

318
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,700
Oh, my God, where's my purse?

319
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,600
No, I can replace everything in there.

320
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:40,360
- Get that binder and let's go!  - Hi.

321
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,820
Some little snacks for everybody.

322
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:46,860
You don't have to eat the sour worms. Those are for Owen.

323
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:49,080
I'll go get him in a second.

324
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:50,600
By the way, you should know,

325
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:52,440
we haven't told him he's adopted yet.

326
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:54,900
But kids are so intuitive.

327
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,960
Don't you think, on some level, he already knows?

328
00:15:58,360 --> 00:16:00,960
- I'm adopted?  - See? Intuitive.

329
00:16:01,780 --> 00:16:03,980
What? Where did you hear that?

330
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,540
He told me.

331
00:16:06,980 --> 00:16:09,860
And he paid me 50 dollars not to tell.

332
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,460
Which, technically, now you should give back.

333
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,760
You told him he's adopted?

334
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:19,880
I'm sorry.

335
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,820
But You should have a sign out there or something.

336
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:24,860
Or at least whisper it to people when they come in the door.

337
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,760
"Owen doesn't know he's adopted,

338
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,700
and he also thinks Santa is real."

339
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,020
He isn't?

340
00:16:32,040 --> 00:16:33,740
We have to get out of here, baby.

341
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,660
Everyone, I would like to make a toast...

342
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,720
...to Rachel and Joey.

343
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:48,700
And to love.

344
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:53,160
Ah, love!

345
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,980
L-O-V-E. Love.

346
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,720
L is for "life."

347
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,100
And what is life without love?

348
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,200
Oh, my God, are we supposed to answer?

349
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:11,020
O is for...

350
00:17:12,526 --> 00:17:13,907
"Oh, wow!"

351
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:20,300
The V is for this...

352
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:23,780
...very surprising turn of events...

353
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:28,560
...which I am still fine with, by the way.

354
00:17:30,405 --> 00:17:31,565
E...

355
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:37,020
...is for how...

356
00:17:37,569 --> 00:17:40,829
...extremely normal I find it...

357
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:42,900
...that you two...

358
00:17:44,929 --> 00:17:46,349
...are together.

359
00:17:48,300 --> 00:17:50,940
And that one day you might get married...

360
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:56,460
...and have children of your own.

361
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:03,220
- Dude, are you okay? - Totally.

362
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,440
Ross, you don't seem okay.

363
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:08,160
I'm sorry,

364
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,000
it must be the pressure of entertaining.

365
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:17,440
I think everyone would feel better if we had some flan.

366
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:22,220
Wait, Ross. Ross, l--I have to take off.

367
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:24,100
- No!  - I'm sorry.

368
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,900
I have an early class in the morning.

369
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:29,600
But this has been lovely.

370
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:35,580
Wasn't it? And you thought it would be awkward with Joey.

371
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:37,760
And that you never really liked Rachel.

372
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:40,320
You are on fire!

373
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,520
I'll call you in the morning, okay?

374
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:44,480
- Okay. - All right.

375
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:50,540
God, Rachel, what Ross just said, that's just--

376
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,480
That's okay. Girls tend not to like me.

377
00:18:53,902 --> 00:18:55,292
Fine.

378
00:18:57,700 --> 00:19:01,280
Okay. I guess it's just flan for three.

379
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:04,580
Hey, that rhymes.

380
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:11,040
You know what, Ross, I think we're gonna take off too.

381
00:19:12,660 --> 00:19:15,340
Of course. God, I'm so stupid.

382
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,660
You guys are a couple now.

383
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,120
I mean, you probably just want to be alone.

384
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,780
No, it's just getting late--

385
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:24,480
It's fine. It's totally fine.

386
00:19:24,480 --> 00:19:26,780
I've got plenty of margaritas. It's all good.

387
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,440
I don't even know what that's for.

388
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:42,620
You know what?

389
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:46,460
I think I'm gonna stay here and make sure he's okay.

390
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:47,960
That's probably a good idea.

391
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:49,360
I'll see you in the morning.

392
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:50,680
Okay.

393
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,820
Yeah, you know, Joey, l--

394
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:56,100
I don't think he's ever gonna

395
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:56,700
be okay with this.

396
00:19:56,720 --> 00:19:58,820
It doesn't look good, does it?

397
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:20,880
Morning.

398
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:23,480
- Here you go.  - Thanks.

399
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:28,320
- Did you stay here all night?  - Yeah.

400
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,480
So you took off my pants and shoes?

401
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:34,400
No...

402
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:36,560
You actually did that when you  were

403
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:38,620
dancing to the <i>Chicago</i> soundtrack.

404
00:20:41,388 --> 00:20:43,978
Look, Ross...

405
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:45,980
...about Rachel and l.

406
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:48,260
Listen, you don't have to worry about that...

407
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,740
...because nothing's gonna happen.

408
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:51,740
What do you mean?

409
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,500
She and I said from the beginning...

410
00:20:55,780 --> 00:20:56,780
...we weren't gonna do anything

411
00:20:56,980 --> 00:20:58,500
unless you were okay with it.

412
00:20:58,516 --> 00:21:00,006
And clearly--

413
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:02,180
What are you talking about? I'm fine.

414
00:21:03,540 --> 00:21:07,360
It's okay, Ross. You know, I totally understand.

415
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:09,440
Of course you're not fine. You're...

416
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,480
You're Ross and Rachel.

417
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,200
Yeah, except we're not.

418
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:23,460
I mean, we haven't been a couple in, like...

419
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:25,700
...six years.

420
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,040
My God, is that right?

421
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:32,800
Has it been that long?

422
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:34,920
That's what I hear, yeah.

423
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:40,700
This is crazy.I mean, six years...

424
00:21:41,020 --> 00:21:43,780
...and because of me, you guys aren't gonna be together?

425
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,120
Can I ask you something?

426
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:49,500
Really...

427
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:53,160
...what is this thing with you and Rachel?

428
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:58,000
Come on, you know me. You know...

429
00:22:00,820 --> 00:22:01,260
Joey.

430
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:10,200
I'm crazy about her.

431
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:17,260
And she feels the same way?

432
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:21,120
I think so.

433
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:25,700
Well, then...

434
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,620
...maybe it's time we all moved on.

435
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:32,060
Yeah, but, Ross, I mean, you're not okay with it, so--

436
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:35,200
No, but I want to be.

437
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:38,600
I will be.

438
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:44,260
Besides, I'm with Charlie, right?

439
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:47,880
Oh, my God, I'm still with Charlie, aren't l?

440
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,460
- She didn't see the dance, did she?  - No...

441
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:54,260
No, that was--That was just for me.

442
00:22:58,940 --> 00:22:59,580
Hey, you...?

443
00:23:01,160 --> 00:23:02,020
You sure about this?

444
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,420
Yeah, I'm sure.

445
00:23:08,061 --> 00:23:08,870
And...

446
00:23:10,263 --> 00:23:12,002
...we're okay?

447
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:25,100
- Hey, Pheebs. - Hey.

448
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:27,360
We just want to give you a heads up.

449
00:23:27,840 --> 00:23:29,780
- Bill and Colleen hate us.  - Why?

450
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:31,180
Owen didn't know he's adopted

451
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:32,360
and Monica told him.

452
00:23:32,480 --> 00:23:33,350
What?

453
00:23:34,120 --> 00:23:35,800
Still, he had to find out sometime.

454
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:37,120
How would you like it

455
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:38,080
if someone told the triplets

456
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:39,380
that you gave birth to them?

457
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:45,720
I'm gonna go tell Emma

458
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:46,480
she was an accident.

